Read root `AGENTS.md` first. It is the product, scope, architecture, workflow, and validation source of truth shared by Cursor, Codex, and other agents. Do not duplicate or override it here.

Cursor essentials:

- This is an Unreal Engine C++ project for `禍祓い`, not a browser or Unity project. Preserve the fixed four-encounter Campaign and the calm/purification design.
- Make the smallest coherent change. Read relevant source, tests, Docs, and Specs before editing; inspect current `main` and open PRs when access permits.
- Campaign Save/Continue is an existing supported feature. Do not restore the obsolete blanket prohibition on saves; keep its intentionally small chapter-only format unless explicitly asked to change it.
- Use `Tools/Prototype.ps1` for the supported Check, Build, Setup, Play, Test, Package, and Automation/E2E paths when Windows UE is available.
- Run focused Python source-contract tests and then `python -m pytest Tests -q` where possible.
- `Tests/production-gameplay-contract.json` is updated only after an intentional gameplay-source change, only with `python Tools/GameplayContract.py --update`, and never by hand.
- Follow `.clang-format` and existing UE naming. Do not add speculative frameworks or unrelated refactors.
- Never infer UE runtime, rendering, camera, hardware-input, animation, audio, packaged-build, or human-playtest success from headless/static tests. Use the `PASS`, `FAIL`, `NOT_RUN`, and `STATIC_PASS` meanings in `AGENTS.md` and report environmental blockers precisely.
